[109.222901, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[115.449579, "o", "the real model's raw answer (gemma3:1b through Ollama, on this machine):\r\n   Okay, here's a 3-step guide to reconnect your laptop to the office Wi-Fi:\r\n\r\n   1.  **Open Settings:** Click the \"Settings\" icon (usually a gear) on your taskbar or in the Start menu.\r\n   2.  **Network & Internet:**  Select \"Network & Internet\" from the left-hand menu.\r\n   3.  **Connect to Wi-Fi:** Choose your office's Wi-Fi network from the list and click \"Join.\"\r\n\r\n   Let me know if you have any other questions!\r\n"]
[115.450505, "o", "\r\nthe HTML a chat app makes from it (this file's tiny Markdown renderer):\r\n   <p>Okay, here's a 3-step guide to reconnect your laptop to the office Wi-Fi:</p>\r\n   <ol><li><strong>Open Settings:</strong> Click the \"Settings\" icon (usually a gear) on your taskbar or in the Start menu.</li><li><strong>Network & Internet:</strong>  Select \"Network & Internet\" from the left-hand menu.</li><li><strong>Connect to Wi-Fi:</strong> Choose your office's Wi-Fi network from the list and click \"Join.\"</li></ol>\r\n   <p>Let me know if you have any other questions!</p>\r\n\r\n"]
[115.450802, "o", "how a browser reads it (explained by Python's html.parser; no browser runs here):\r\n"]
[115.451158, "o", "   elements: <p> x2, <ol> x1, <li> x3, <strong> x3\r\n   nothing here is fetched or run: only text and formatting\r\n"]
[115.462289, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;thesecguy@lab: ~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m05\u0007\u001b[01;32mthesecguy@lab\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m05\u001b[00m$ "]
